{% from "components/ui.njk" import pageHero, ctaSection with context %}
{{ pageHero("Software-first · Deployment-specific field scope", "PBB deployment model", "PBB is assembled around service ownership, privacy boundaries, local operating capacity, and continuity needs—not a single identical appliance for every site.", null, "deploymentHero") }}
<div class="container detail-sections">
  <section class="detail-section" aria-labelledby="service-classes"><p class="section-kicker">Service classes</p><h2 id="service-classes">Baseline, optional, and specialized</h2><div class="deployment-summary"><article><strong>Baseline</strong><p>Shared services and locally essential capabilities expected in the approved node design.</p></article><article><strong>Optional</strong><p>Daily-use or context-specific modules included when ownership, capacity, and community need support them.</p></article><article><strong>Specialized</strong><p>Operational services placed only where trained roles, authority, and data boundaries justify them.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="detail-section" aria-labelledby="node-placements"><p class="section-kicker">Node placements</p><h2 id="node-placements">Services follow their responsible teams</h2><div class="card-grid">{% for item in deployments.placements %}<article class="module-card"><h3>{{ item.label }}</h3><p>{% if item.id == "barangay-node" %}Community-facing services and local emergency intake near residents.{% elif item.id == "local-command-node" %}Coordination, shared infrastructure, maps, and authorized operational views.{% elif item.id in ["health-center-node", "city-municipal-health-node"] %}Health continuity workflows within approved clinical and privacy boundaries.{% elif item.id == "field-health-node" %}A humanitarian or field node for approved mobile health, relief, and response teams operating near affected communities.{% elif item.id == "daily-apps-node" %}Communication and community services that build familiarity before disruption.{% elif item.id in ["learning-node", "library-node"] %}Local learning and governed knowledge resources near their stewards.{% elif item.id == "utility-operations-node" %}Designated utility incident context and mission coordination.{% elif item.id == "support-node" %}A city or municipal support node for consolidated SITREPs and governed inter-node support-request handling.{% else %}Evacuation registration, occupancy, and relief workflows with trained local ownership.{% endif %}</p></article>{% endfor %}</div></section>
  <section class="detail-section problem-panel" aria-labelledby="commercial-boundary"><p class="section-kicker">Commercial and field boundary</p><h2 id="commercial-boundary">Hardware and field costs are explicit</h2><p>The public software platform does not silently bundle servers, networking, internet or private links, backup power, field equipment, travel, accommodation, installation labor, training, data preparation, support coverage, or recurring third-party services. A proposal must state what is included and price or assign everything else separately.</p></section>
  <section class="detail-section" aria-labelledby="deployment-flow"><p class="section-kicker">Structured deployment</p><h2 id="deployment-flow">From discovery to accepted operation</h2><ol class="workflow-steps"><li><span class="step-number">1</span><div><h3>Discover</h3><p>Confirm services, users, authority, data boundaries, sites, hazards, network conditions, and operating ownership.</p></div></li><li><span class="step-number">2</span><div><h3>Design</h3><p>Select node placements, topology, hardware, power, security controls, backups, and deployment-specific integrations.</p></div></li><li><span class="step-number">3</span><div><h3>Prepare and validate</h3><p>Install verified artifacts, prepare local resources, test disconnected behavior, train operators, and exercise recovery.</p></div></li><li><span class="step-number">4</span><div><h3>Pilot and accept</h3><p>Use agreed acceptance criteria, support coverage, incident procedures, evidence, and owner sign-off before expansion.</p></div></li></ol></section>
